cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the manuscript below; cite the repository release for the artifact."
title: "ZeeBeam: The Zero-Knowledge Beam"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Hynes
    given-names: Cathal Ryan
    affiliation: PolieBotics
repository-code: "https://github.com/poliebotics/zeebeam"
license-url: "https://github.com/poliebotics/zeebeam/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  ZeeBeam is the projector-camera capture-and-proof system, and a ZeeBeam recording is a session with rows proved
  under it; the work belongs to Dark Lantern, the wider privacy and zero-knowledge research programme. This
  repository holds one ZeeBeam recording. For each of 259 anchored rows of a 712-row session, one SP1 zkVM program wrapped in
  Groth16 proves that the drand quicknet signatures of the row's round and the preceding round verify, that the
  BLAKE3 chain state was advanced as specified, that the pattern supplied to the coupling computation derives
  from that state, that two frozen integer neural networks produced the published outputs on the committed frame,
  that the row is a leaf of the committed session tree, and that a supplied Zcash v6 transaction, recomputed from
  raw bytes with its Merkle branch checked to a supplied block header, carries a memo whose decrypted binding equals
  SHA-256 of a receipt that opens a chameleon commitment over the chain-log prefix containing the row;
  canonical-mainnet status of that header is an out-of-band check. A
  second program proves the whole chain log against the beacon. Every raw Groth16 proof is 356 bytes; final-relation
  row statements are 1,101 bytes, the two previous-revision statements 1,085 bytes and the chain statement 279 bytes,
  and none contains pixels. The release also holds the manuscript after nineteen referee passes by a second model,
  two companions, the frozen source with fail-closed build drivers, the standalone verifier and the referee trail.
keywords:
  - ZeeBeam
  - Dark Lantern
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - zkVM
  - SP1
  - Groth16
  - drand
  - BLAKE3
  - Zcash
  - projector-camera capture
  - capture provenance
